            "sourceLimit": "RP9.1 supports the coordinate-bonding core at LK. The whole existing Fehling/tartrate and supplied qualitative occupied-donor/unoccupied-acceptor orbital case is a declared own operational foundation, not exact official whole-profile credit. No choice of9.2/8.7 or full optional orbital/complex theory module is inferred.",
            "acquisitionScope": "Whole unchanged363c/P: ligand lone pair and supplied suitable central-ion acceptor orbital, soluble Cu(II)-tartrate purpose, coordination versus later Cu(II)/Cu(I) redox, fresh donor availability and fragment-model limits. This model explanation gives no actual Fehling experiment or EDTA titration credit.",
            "routeBoundary": "The coordination model requires explaining a shared electron pair and distinguishing coordination from redox. The revised direct teachers are existing bond types4488 and redox concepts04fa. Complete aldehyde/ketone assay execution973c and the full supplied EPA-angle course9b56 are not universal prior performances of this qualitative fragment-model capability. All their own authored targets, profiles and actual execution duties remain unchanged. No laboratory execution or EDTA titration is credited by a coordination diagram. Exact changed source/applicability and final native context bindings remain pending."
